  -lang  <str> choose language (valid choices:
     apex, bash, c, c#, c++, cairo, circom, clojure, cpp, csharp, dart, docker, dockerfile, elixir, ex, fga, generic, go, golang, gosu, hack, hcl, html, java, javascript, js, json, jsonnet, julia, kotlin, kt, lisp, lua, move_on_aptos, move_on_sui, none, ocaml, openfga, php, powershell, promql, proto, proto3, protobuf, py, python, python2, python3, r, regex, ruby, rust, scala, scheme, sh, sol, solidity, swift, terraform, tf, ts, typescript, vue, xml, yaml)
  -l  <str> shortcut for -lang
  -j  <int> number of cores to use (default: automatic)
  -json  output JSON format
  -json_nodots  output JSON format but without intermediate dots
  -json_time  report detailed matching times as part of the JSON response. Implies '-json'.
  -fail_fast  stop at first exception (and get a backtrace)
  -filter_irrelevant_patterns  filter patterns not containing any strings in target file
  -no_filter_irrelevant_patterns  do not filter patterns
  -filter_irrelevant_rules  filter rules not containing any strings in target file
  -no_filter_irrelevant_rules  do not filter rules
  -fast  filter rules not containing any strings in target file
  -disable_rule_paths  do not honor the paths: directive of the rule
  -tree_sitter_only  only use tree-sitter-based parsers
  -pfff_only  only use pfff-based parsers
  -timeout  <float> maxinum time to spend running a rule on a single file (in seconds); 0 disables timeouts (default is 0)
  -timeout_threshold  <int> maximum number of rules that can timeout on a file before the file is skipped; 0 disables it (default is 0)
  -max_memory <int>  maximum memory available (in MiB); allows for clean termination when running out of memory. This value should be less than the actual memory available because the limit will be exceeded before it gets detected. Try 5% less or 15000 if you have 16 GB.
  -max_tainted_vars <int> maximum number of vars to store. This is mostly for internal use to make performance testing easier
  -max_taint_set_size <int> maximum size of a taint set. This is mostly for internal use to make performance testing easier
  -max_match_per_file  <int> maximum numbers of match per file
  -debug  output debugging information
  -strict  fail on warnings
  -debug_matching  raise an exception at the first match failure
  -matching_explanations  output intermediate matching explanations
  -log_to_file  <file> log debugging info to file
  -trace  output tracing information
  -trace_endpoint  url endpoint for collecting tracing information
  -macros  <file> list of macros to expand
  -profile  record and output profiling information to stderr
  -simple_profiling  record profiling information for inclusion in JSON results
  -show_trace_profile  show trace
  -debugger  option to set if launched inside ocamldebug
  -keep_tmp_files  keep temporary generated files
  -full_token_info  print also token information in dumper
  -check_rules  <metachecks file> <files or dirs>
